Date: 2023-10-13
Num: 1
Issue: TRANS99 - Error writing file (RC = 6): file transfer canceled

Downloaded CMS Pipelines Runtime Distribution, failed to upload RTDOC VMARC
because it is too large to store in a CDF file (~89K records).

Test:
IND$FILE PUT RTDOC VMARC

Fix:
Split RTDOC VMARC using splitdoc.bat into RTDOC1 VMARC (PDF and PS files) and
RTDOC2 VMARC (all the other files).

NOTE: RTDOC1 shouldn't need to be uploaded to CMS.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Date: 2024-04-29
Num: 2
Issue: CMS Pipelines needs to be NUCXLOADed.

Appendix D "Running Multiple Versions" of SL26-0018-06 "CMS/TSO Pipelines
Author's Edition 1.1.12" says to load the Pipelines back-end (PIPELINE MODULE)
as follows:

    Assuming you are running with the Program Offering level of CMS Pipelines
    and you wish to try some commands against the pipeline shipped in Virtual
    Machine/Enterprise Systems Architecture, you can issue these commands to
    make an EPIPE command:

    nucxload epipmod dmspipe (system service immcmd
    epipmod install epipe

VM/370 CMS does not have a NUCXLOAD command, or relocatable MODULEs.

Test:
None

Fix:
Wrote RPSNXL ASSEMBLE to NUCXLOAD a relocatable module, as close to how CMS/SP5
would as possible.

NOTE: There is no documentation on the relocation data in a MODULE file.
      This support might not work for other MODULEs.  See the big warning at
      the top of RPSNXL ASSEMBLE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Date: 2024-05-12
Num: 3
Issue: DMSZAP056E FILE 'PIPELINE MODULE' CONTAINS INVALID RECORD FORMATS.

The ZAP command issues message "DMSZAP056E FILE 'PIPELINE MODULE' CONTAINS
INVALID RECORD FORMATS." and refuses to apply any ZAPs.  The problem is
that ZAP can't handle relocatable MODULE files.

Test:
ZAP MODULE (NOPRINT INPUT PLUNGE01

Fix:
Wrote PLUCMD ASSEMBLE, to clear the clogs and make PIPEs run clean :-)
Must be run and "ENABLE"d before first PIPE command is issued.

Rather than write relocatable MODULE support for ZAP, I wrote a wrapper around
NUCXLOAD to apply ZAPs to the MODULE in memory.  Implemented as PLUZAP
ASSEMBLE.

NOTE: This code uses a reserved word at NUCON+x'FFC' to hold a pointer to a
      workarea (NUCPLUPT).  Nothing else in the virtual machine can use it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Date: 2024-05-13
Num: 4
Issue: FPLINY1291I The field ADMSCWR in NUCON is incorrect; found 00F8C158;
display of ABEND information may be in jeopardy.

Update HRC415DS moved the CMS nucleus to high memory, but didn't set NUCALPHA,
NUCSIGMA, and NUCOMEGA, so Pipelines thinks DMSCWR (WRTERM) isn't where it
should be.  Pipelines doesn't change any behavior, it just issues the message.
Since we can't control where DMSCWR is located, we suppress the message
instead.

Test:
NUCXTEXT NUCXLOAD RPSNXL (SYSTEM
NUCXLOAD PIPMOD PIPELINE (SYSTEM SERVICE IMMCMD
PIPMOD INSTALL PIPE

Fix:
Wrote ZAP001 in PLUZAP ASSEMBLE to not issue the message.

