Date: 2024-06-23
Num: 8
Issue: Incorrect detection of machine mode.

PIPMOD tests NUCMFLAG to determine what sort of CMS it is running in.  But that
byte was originally DCSSFLG in VM/370, until it was turned into a spare byte
in VM/SP, and later re-used.

Test:
None

Fix:
Wrote ZAP003 in PLUZAP ASSEMBLE to use reserved NUCON field NUCCFA, which has
always been unused, and lets PIPMOD set either NUCMEC or NUCM370 in it,
depending on whether CMS is running in EC mode or not.  There turn out to lots
of these.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Date: 2024-07-10
Num: 9
Issue: DIAG 0 needs VM/SP bit.

Because DIAG 0 in VM/370 doesn't set the "VM/SP" bit, PIPMOD's
conditionl logic thinks it's running under VM/XA.

Test:
None, discovered while fixing issue 8.

Fix:
Wrote ZAP004 in PLUZAP ASSEMBLE to issue SVC 199 instead of DIAG 0.

Added an SVC first-level interrupt handler (SVCHND) to PLUCMD ASSEMBLE, because
CMS's HNDSVC is reset at the end of every command.

Added SVC 199 code (S199D00) to PLUCMD ASSEMBLE to issue the DIAG and set the
VM/SP bit before returning.

WARNING: This code is called directly from the SVC New PSW, so it
         sees EVERY SVC instruction, and must be fast and careful.

